# K03d, migrated by K03-EXPLICIT-RECEIVER-FRAMES.  This row pinned `copy: merge Model` at the unit's
# root, the atom spelling the author (2026-10-06) calls a typo; it is the Frame `copy: merge: Model`.
# The merge result is declared at the unit's top level, and `read` names the free `copy\value`.  By the
# general priority of a free name's sources the method's hidden input is that result (K02c,
# MERGE-HIDDEN-INPUT-PROJECTION), so read returns 1.  The atom spelling's reading -- a settle into
# this Frame -- is gone with the other atom readings.
# Success is 7.
Model: (int: value 1)
copy: merge: Model
fn: read () int
return: copy\value

int: result read()
if: result != 1
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
